course: dictionary
lesson: 13196
title: Fugitive: running away or fleeting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A fugitive is a person who is running away or hiding, often from the police or from danger. «The fugitive ran across the field and hid in the woods.» The clues are ran, hid and woods. Someone who is escaping and hiding is a fugitive.
explain: Fugitive can also be an adjective, a describing word, that means running away or escaping. «The fugitive horse broke through the gate and galloped off down the lane.» Here the horse is the one escaping, so fugitive tells you how it is moving.
explain: In some books, fugitive means lasting only a short time. «A fugitive smile crossed her face before it vanished.» Her smile came and went very quickly. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A fugitive is someone who runs away or hides to escape from something.
fact: «Fugitive» can be a noun, as in «a fugitive», or an adjective, as in «a fugitive horse».
fact: «Fugitive» can also mean lasting only a short time, like «a fugitive smile».
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad becomes a fugitive after escaping from prison.
fact: Clues such as ran, hid and police help you work out that a fugitive is escaping.
exercise: «The fugitive ran across the field and hid in the woods.» Who is the fugitive? | A tree that grows tall | *A person running away and hiding | A bird that sings in the woods | A farmer who owns the field
exercise: «The fugitive smile lasted only a second.» What does fugitive mean here? | Painted on a wall | Very big and bright | *Lasting only a short time
exercise: «Police searched the town for the fugitive.» What was the fugitive probably doing? | Baking a cake for a party | Singing in a school choir | *Running away from the police | Sleeping in a warm bed
test: «The fugitive horse broke through the gate and galloped off down the lane.» What does fugitive mean in «a fugitive horse»? | Sleepy and slow | Brown and spotted | Tall and thin | *Running away or escaping
test: «The fugitive hid in the old barn for three days.» What is a fugitive? | A type of hay | A loud noise at night | A kind helper on a farm | *A person hiding to escape from danger
exam: «The fugitive hid behind the old barn, hoping no one would find him.» What does fugitive mean here? | A friendly neighbour who visits | *A person who is running away and hiding | A lost dog that wants to be found | A bright light in the dark
